import java.io.*;
import java.net.*;
import javax.net.*;
import javax.net.ssl.*;
import java.security.*;
public class SSLServer {
 public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
 SSLServerSocketFactory sslServerSocketFactory = (SSLServerSocketFactory)SSLServerSocketFactory.getDefault();
 SSLServerSocket sslServerSocket = (SSLServerSocket)sslServerSocketFactory.createServerSocket(8888);
 SSLSocket sslSocket = (SSLSocket)sslServerSocket.accept();
 BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(sslSocket.getInputStream()));
 PrintWriter out = new PrintWriter(sslSocket.getOutputStream(), true);
 out.println("Hello, client!");
 String inputLine = in.readLine();
 System.out.println("Received message from client: " + inputLine);
 in.close();
 out.close();
 sslSocket.close();
 }
}
```
Client-side code:
```
import java.io.*;
import java.net.*;
import javax.net.*;
import javax.net.ssl.*;
import java.security.*;
public class SSLClient {
 public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
 SSLSocketFactory sslSocketFactory = (SSLSocketFactory)SSLSocketFactory.getDefault();
 SSLSocket sslSocket = (SSLSocket)sslSocketFactory.createSocket("localhost", 8888);
 BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(sslSocket.getInputStream()));
 PrintWriter out = new PrintWriter(sslSocket.getOutputStream(), true);
 String inputLine = in.readLine();
 System.out.println("Received message from server: " + inputLine);
 out.println("Hello, server!");
 in.close();
 out.close();
 sslSocket.close();
 }
}
```
As for the three network security protocols that can be utilized to establish a secure connection between two devices, here they are:
1. SSL/TLS - Secure Sockets Layer/Transport Layer Security is a protocol that provides secure communication over the internet. It encrypts data transmitted between two devices and ensures that it cannot be intercepted or tampered with.
2. IPSec - Internet Protocol Security is a protocol suite that provides security services for IP networks. It provides authentication, encryption, and integrity protection for IP packets.
3. SSH - Secure Shell is a protocol that provides secure remote access to a device. It encrypts all traffic between the client and server, and provides authentication and integrity protection.

